{
  "family": "capabilityGateLaws",
  "kitVersion": "0.43.0",
  "description": "The capability registry's gate, decision context and grant (Phase 638, DECISIONS.md D249), as data a port decides from (Phase 650, D255). Authored inputs, each `expected` computed by calling the pinned kit; no seed. `registry` holds the three capability declarations, each a canonical declaration as a JSON string. `contexts` names the two decision contexts, opaque labels. `gates` is the gate table in the order the registry runs it: a gate answers the `decision` of its rule for the (context, capability) pair, and `allow` for any pair it has no rule for. The registry's decision is the join over every gate in order (allow < needsApproval < deny, a deny keeping its message and alternatives), and the gate that made it is the FIRST gate whose decision has the greatest rank; `policy` is \"\" when every gate allows. `invocationIdentity` vectors expect the identity a grant is bound to: the fields id, then for each binding its address and its value's canonical spelling in its hole's space (an integer without sign or leading zeros, a number in its shortest round-trip form, a string as given), the bindings sorted by address (ordinal), each field written with every U+0010 and U+0001 it holds preceded by U+0010, then terminated by U+0001; no hash is taken. `grantCovers` vectors expect whether a presented grant (the `grant` member, an identity; absent when none is presented) is for exactly this invocation: it is when the two identities are equal as strings. `decideNamed` vectors expect the registry's named decision for an invocation under a context with a grant presented: `decided` with the deciding gate and the decision, where a needsApproval a covering grant lifts is `allow` and keeps the gate's name, and no grant lifts a deny; or, where no gate decided, `refused` with the refusal a dispatch gives (an unregistered id is `noSuchCapability` with the registered ids, an argument out of its space `argOutOfSpace`). `dispatch` vectors expect `performed` when the performer ran, exactly once, or `refused` with the refusal: `policyRefused` naming the gate with its reason and alternatives for a deny, `approvalRequired` naming the gate for a needsApproval no grant lifts, `noSuchCapability` for an unregistered id whatever is presented; a refused dispatch never runs the performer. `referenceOnly` names the cases no extracted model answers, with the reason.",
  "registry": ["{\"$type\":\"capability\",\"determinism\":\"deterministic\",\"id\":\"erase\",\"placement\":{\"$type\":\"server\"},\"result\":{\"$type\":\"nothing\"},\"signature\":{\"effect\":{\"determinism\":\"deterministic\",\"host\":\"pure\"},\"holes\":[{\"addr\":\"n\",\"kind\":\"value\",\"name\":\"n\",\"required\":true,\"space\":{\"$type\":\"intRange\",\"max\":99,\"min\":0}}],\"name\":\"erase\"}}", "{\"$type\":\"capability\",\"determinism\":\"deterministic\",\"id\":\"read\",\"placement\":{\"$type\":\"server\"},\"result\":{\"$type\":\"intRange\",\"max\":99,\"min\":0},\"signature\":{\"effect\":{\"determinism\":\"deterministic\",\"host\":\"pure\"},\"holes\":[{\"addr\":\"n\",\"kind\":\"value\",\"name\":\"n\",\"required\":true,\"space\":{\"$type\":\"intRange\",\"max\":99,\"min\":0}}],\"name\":\"read\"}}", "{\"$type\":\"capability\",\"determinism\":\"deterministic\",\"id\":\"write\",\"placement\":{\"$type\":\"server\"},\"result\":{\"$type\":\"nothing\"},\"signature\":{\"effect\":{\"determinism\":\"deterministic\",\"host\":\"pure\"},\"holes\":[{\"addr\":\"n\",\"kind\":\"value\",\"name\":\"n\",\"required\":true,\"space\":{\"$type\":\"intRange\",\"max\":99,\"min\":0}},{\"addr\":\"x\",\"kind\":\"value\",\"name\":\"x\",\"required\":true,\"space\":{\"$type\":\"floatRange\",\"max\":10,\"min\":0}},{\"addr\":\"s\",\"kind\":\"value\",\"name\":\"s\",\"required\":true,\"space\":{\"$type\":\"anyString\"}}],\"name\":\"write\"}}"],
  "contexts": ["trusted", "untrusted"],
  "gates": [{ "policy": "ceiling", "rules": [{ "context": "untrusted", "capability": "write", "decision": "needsApproval" }, { "context": "untrusted", "capability": "erase", "decision": "deny", "message": "erasing is not open to this context", "alternatives": ["read"] }, { "context": "trusted", "capability": "erase", "decision": "needsApproval" }] }, { "policy": "audit", "rules": [{ "context": "untrusted", "capability": "write", "decision": "needsApproval" }, { "context": "untrusted", "capability": "erase", "decision": "needsApproval" }, { "context": "trusted", "capability": "write", "decision": "needsApproval" }, { "context": "trusted", "capability": "erase", "decision": "deny", "message": "an erase is held for the audit", "alternatives": [] }] }],
  "referenceOnly": [{ "case": "decideNamed", "reason": "the model states the gates' join and the grant's lift (decide_named, grant_lifted in proofs/Capability.fst) and proves them, but neither is extracted, so no oracle function answers a decision" }, { "case": "dispatch", "reason": "the model's gated dispatch (dispatch_gated) is stated and proved over the same unextracted join, and no oracle function runs it" }],
